# Git workflow

One logical step per commit.

Before commit:

- inspect git diff
- run relevant validation
- verify no secrets
- verify no generated cache
- verify no accidental unrelated changes

Do not commit unfinished UI simply because coding finished.
UI implementation must first be visually approved.
Once the user approves: commit → push → next step.

Initial project setup may be committed after successful verification.

Never force push. Never modify origin unless explicitly requested.
